From a34f9c858b3a357332e55b31ae52ae5a4d73b125 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:44:09 +0000
Subject: ipa: soft: Lift the shadows with a dark boost

The tuning's DRC tone mapping lifts the shadows by the DRC gain and a
fixed dark boost offset. Qualcomm's ADRC also has AEC measure the
darkest pixels and, when they sit below a floor, ask for a dark boost
gain the tone mapping lifts them by on top (TMC 1.2's DRCGainDark);
exposure does not change for it.

With histogram darkRef, darkRange and maxDarkBoost, have Agc measure
the darkest pixels as the tone curve will have lifted them by the DRC
gain, and set a dark boost of up to maxDarkBoost to bring them to
darkRef, filtered as the DRC gain is. Adjust builds the DRC curve with
it, through the anchors' darkBoostRatio. How Qualcomm's AEC computes
its gain is not public; the floor, pixel range and bound are its
tuning's.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
